    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In this case, the corresponding index is known as the “half-index” (of Neumann boundary condition) [14]. Due to an obvious symmetry between t and u, the limit t → 0 is essentially same as u → 0. However, in the analysis in the next subsection, these two limits look different, and lead to the equivalent result non-trivially."
