    "content" : "We stress that all of them are obtained from the index (2.10) as special limits. The reduced index IN(t,u;q) is regarded as a two-parameter deformation of the Schur index IN(q1/2,q1/2;q). As mentioned in the introductory section, we refer to IN(t,u;q) as the deformed Schur index."
